# The build stage does `COPY . .` and then `go build`, so anything here that is
# not Go source is dead weight sent to the daemon on every build.
#
# /workspace is the one that matters. It holds every agent's working tree, and
# agents clone into theirs — a single conversation that checked out a Go
# toolchain took the build context past 7G. It is bind-mounted at run time from
# the host anyway, so the image never wanted it.

# Per-agent workspaces, databases and session transcripts.
/workspace/

# Secrets — the runtime gets these through env_file, not the image.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# Local config, bind-mounted at run time.
roundclaw.yaml

# Built binaries — the image builds its own.
/worker
/gateway

.git/
